  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cultivating village pregnancy and childbirth care workers to promote maternal and child health for women with disabilities in Vientiane, Laos</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Increase access to maternal and child health services for mothers and postpartum women with disabilities through the opening of a center for the promotion of maternal and child health for women with disabilities. -Checking the needs of women with disabilities for maternity health-related services and creating a safe pregnancy and childbirth environment through community-oriented visitation services and case management of pregnancy and childbirth care agents. -Training pregnancy and childbirth care workers as leaders of self-help groups in the village, helping women with disabilities develop their capacity to manage pregnancy and childbirth independently. -Recruitment and education of trainees, including women with disabilities, provide opportunities for universal education for the underprivileged. -Contributing to promoting maternal and child health of women with disabilities by strengthening health service capabilities and improving the quality of maternal and child health services</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to cultivate village pregnancy and childbirth care workers to promote maternal and child health for women with disabilities in Vientiane Laos in connection with Strengthening the health system for better maternal and child health services promoted by KOICA Establish a community service operating system for maternal and child health for women with disabilities&#xbaa8;&#xc790;&#xbcf4;&#xac74; &#xc0b0;&#xc804;&#xc0b0;&#xd6c4;&#xad00;&#xb9ac; &#xc778;&#xc2dd; &#xc81c;&#xace0;
&#xc784;&#xc2e0;&#xcd9c;&#xc0b0;&#xcf00;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;&#xc6d0;&#xc758; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9; &#xac15;&#xd654;</narrative>
  </description>
